<!--Render Target Documentation — HelperFunctions
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation.HelperFunctions-->
<rdoc:HelperFunctions xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:rdoc="com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    Which values are computed in SCAD versus in the compiler
  </is>
  <documentation>
    Some helpers run at SCAD render time instead of being precomputed.

    Decided — SCAD runtime:
    - mb_assembly(config, settings, size, direction)
    - mb_assembly_tongue(assembly, renderGroups, group)
    - mb_assembly_groove(assembly, renderGroups, group)
    - mb_assembly_offset(offset, assembly, renderGroups, group)
    - mb_group_render(renderGroups, group)
    - mb_block_id(blockId, partId)
    - mb_parts_total_size(parts)

    The assembly helpers and mb_group_render read assembly mode or
    renderGroups.

    mb_block_id is str(blockId, "/", part). blockId comes from
    mb_param_id(config, settings, fqn) and can be overridden from outside, so
    the renderer emits the call. NativeBlock documents the part id as
    "blockId/partName".

    Decided — mb_params_filter(baseAdjustment, namespace, overrides?):
    The parameter name is baseAdjustment. Core 3.0.0 renamed it from
    baseSideAdjustment. When the map is the runtime parameter (config or
    customizer), emit the call. When the map is a static literal, emit the
    filtered pseudo-map. The optional third argument applies fixed overrides
    after the namespace filter. Entries without a namespace and entries with
    numeric keys are ignored.

    mb_parts_total_size(parts) is the Core SCAD bounding box of the parts
    after direction resolution. Each entry is [id, size, direction, offset].
    id is required. size, direction, and offset are indexes 1, 2, and 3.
    A STEPS row uses that same layout. A composite emits:

        size = mb_parts_total_size(parts);

    A set passes STEPS to the same function:

        ["size", mb_parts_total_size(STEPS)]

    Rule: render-dependent values (assembly, renderGroups, overridable
    blockId) resolve at SCAD runtime. Structural and static values are
    precomputed in MBOM.

  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="rdoc:SerializationRules" relation="ReadNext" />
  </references>
</rdoc:HelperFunctions>
